word-parallel bitmap evaluation with complexity
\(O(\frac{N}{w}(|\mathcal U_Q|+d))\), and homomorphic
aggregation over the matched record set
\(\mathcal R_Q\), requiring \(O(|\mathcal R_Q|)\).
Finally, response verification validates the Merkle proofs
for the matched canonical nodes together with one
blockchain-authenticated epoch commitment, resulting in
\(O(|\mathcal U_Q|+1)\).

Consequently, BVCRSA avoids linear ciphertext scanning by
combining logarithmic canonical-node decomposition,
bitmap-based conjunctive evaluation, bitmap-aware
encrypted aggregation, and authenticated query-state
verification, making it well suited for large-scale
outsourced IIoT analytics.
